    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The bureaucratic circus masters in Brussels have been sharpening their billion-euro pencil for over two years, all because a technology company decided its own shopping, flight, and hotel units deserved the top spots in search results. After swatting away the search giant's fix-it attempts, the verdict is now set to drop before the summer holidays—a headline-grabbing mega-fine is on its way, adding another chapter to the long-running saga of antitrust fines.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
